  'Evolutionary biology explains how genetic variation, selection, drift, history, and ecology shape biological diversity. The syllabus combines population genetics, adaptation, speciation, phylogenetics, macroevolution, molecular evolution, and applied evolutionary thinking.',
  $evobiozzjs${"slug": "evolutionary-biology", "title": "Evolutionary Biology", "description": "Evolutionary biology explains how genetic variation, selection, drift, history, and ecology shape biological diversity. The syllabus combines population genetics, adaptation, speciation, phylogenetics, macroevolution, molecular evolution, and applied evolutionary thinking.", "topics": [{"id": "09199ff1-0915-4bea-86c1-e6abe8082e6b", "type": "topic", "title": "Evidence and history of evolutionary thought", "description": "This module establishes evidence and history of evolutionary thought as the course's first working framework. It supplies the language and representations needed before the path advances to genetic variation.", "children": [{"id": "84a83d41-aa3e-491a-ad70-021659a235e1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Common ancestry", "children": [], "description": "Common ancestry identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within evidence and history of evolutionary thought. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before deep time because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "e158f576-70bf-45dd-9889-65934239e2da", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deep time", "children": [], "description": "Deep time identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within evidence and history of evolutionary thought. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After common ancestry, deep time supplies what is needed to address testable predictions."}, {"id": "b7f6a16b-002b-4e73-90aa-c99f0efaf872", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Testable predictions", "children": [], "description": "Testable predictions identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within evidence and history of evolutionary thought. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, testable predictions carries the completed idea into genetic variation."}]}, {"id": "dff6bb43-795d-486d-a743-be98fd301c19", "type": "topic", "title": "Genetic variation", "description": "This module builds directly on evidence and history of evolutionary thought and develops genetic variation. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for hardy–weinberg framework.", "children": [{"id": "2a54c79b-7370-4500-824e-870c66d4ccf7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mutation", "children": [], "description": "Mutation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within genetic variation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before recombination because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "6cbffa33-f736-4cae-8ec4-22c305000670", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Recombination", "children": [], "description": "Recombination identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within genetic variation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After mutation, recombination supplies what is needed to address genotype/phenotype."}, {"id": "c3099e7b-a4ae-4791-9858-f1a9dc0abcd2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Genotype/phenotype", "children": [], "description": "Genotype/phenotype identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within genetic variation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After recombination, genotype/phenotype supplies what is needed to address molecular variation."}, {"id": "0d630f83-3a5d-4dd9-b6e9-cf10daba25ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Molecular variation", "children": [], "description": "Molecular variation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within genetic variation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, molecular variation carries the completed idea into hardy–weinberg framework."}]}, {"id": "78842f82-0c07-4172-8e1b-6a2ffb613928", "type": "topic", "title": "Hardy–Weinberg framework", "description": "This module builds directly on genetic variation and develops hardy–weinberg framework. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for selection.", "children": [{"id": "8a869cbf-4521-4e7a-a772-e550e9851496", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Allele/genotype frequencies", "children": [], "description": "Allele/genotype frequencies identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within hardy–weinberg framework. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before assumptions because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "90f82057-4da7-486e-a88a-e69cadd1455c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Assumptions", "children": [], "description": "Assumptions identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within hardy–weinberg framework. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After allele/genotype frequencies, assumptions supplies what is needed to address diagnostic use."}, {"id": "4bebda4a-b4c6-4981-a56b-02d79c1bba7f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diagnostic use", "children": [], "description": "Diagnostic use makes the validity limits of hardy–weinberg framework explicit, showing when an otherwise correct method or system can become unreliable. As the final topic in this module, diagnostic use carries the completed idea into selection."}]}, {"id": "fb9897b5-b463-4587-adfc-cd19d47c8e0b", "type": "topic", "title": "Selection", "description": "This module builds directly on hardy–weinberg framework and develops selection. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for drift and effective population size.", "children": [{"id": "1bbdd576-2f21-4a41-9653-12d6062987f7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fitness", "children": [], "description": "Fitness is a governing quantity in selection, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. It appears before dominance because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "2c53d560-a809-43ca-8031-070ade694fc2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dominance", "children": [], "description": "Dominance identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within selection. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After fitness, dominance supplies what is needed to address balancing/directional selection."}, {"id": "819d713a-de56-4e7f-b1aa-834cc060747b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Balancing/directional selection", "children": [], "description": "Balancing/directional selection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within selection. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After dominance, balancing/directional selection supplies what is needed to address response to selection."}, {"id": "0c78f2e3-0c04-46d8-8054-31dc479ba3e7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Response to selection", "children": [], "description": "Response to selection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within selection. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, response to selection carries the completed idea into drift and effective population size."}]}, {"id": "babed2fb-682c-4ede-805e-de21636ce49d", "type": "topic", "title": "Drift and effective population size", "description": "This module builds directly on selection and develops drift and effective population size. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for gene flow and population structure.", "children": [{"id": "61db5402-c06a-4105-a837-c8eecfdc1f4d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fixation", "children": [], "description": "Fixation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within drift and effective population size. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before bottlenecks because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "7a1d8da1-2a87-498d-bd07-515c2f944c05", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bottlenecks", "children": [], "description": "Bottlenecks identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within drift and effective population size. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After fixation, bottlenecks supplies what is needed to address founder effects."}, {"id": "0922986c-8302-49f0-b68f-da91eb950769", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Founder effects", "children": [], "description": "Founder effects identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within drift and effective population size. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After bottlenecks, founder effects supplies what is needed to address coalescent intuition."}, {"id": "6db849dd-e1ed-4dfe-b03a-125f02ff8078", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Coalescent intuition", "children": [], "description": "Coalescent intuition identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within drift and effective population size. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, coalescent intuition carries the completed idea into gene flow and population structure."}]}, {"id": "7e93f407-0bbb-4d97-96fe-a232e2d93609", "type": "topic", "title": "Gene flow and population structure", "description": "This module builds directly on drift and effective population size and develops gene flow and population structure. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for quantitative traits.", "children": [{"id": "edc07607-28d4-4eb3-9d2d-6062a59bd878", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Migration", "children": [], "description": "Migration identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within gene flow and population structure. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before f-statistics concepts because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "32d1d434-bdd6-4324-adbb-e31542bcdc0c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "F-statistics concepts", "children": [], "description": "F-statistics concepts identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within gene flow and population structure. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After migration, f-statistics concepts supplies what is needed to address local adaptation."}, {"id": "6ce2fd56-4b49-40bc-99e5-1cff4bb815c0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Local adaptation", "children": [], "description": "Local adaptation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within gene flow and population structure. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, local adaptation carries the completed idea into quantitative traits."}]}, {"id": "e24da1db-0344-427e-a4cc-b8729a7a1fff", "type": "topic", "title": "Quantitative traits", "description": "This module builds directly on gene flow and population structure and develops quantitative traits. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for phylogenetics.", "children": [{"id": "7eccb635-fcfd-431a-9f2a-3bcef51086a5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Heritability", "children": [], "description": "Heritability identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within quantitative traits. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before breeder’s equation because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "1ed8aaa7-a92d-4b15-a584-d4a2fa674619", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Breeder’s equation", "children": [], "description": "Breeder’s equation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within quantitative traits. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After heritability, breeder’s equation supplies what is needed to address genetic correlations."}, {"id": "510b2694-3fdc-4a2d-a6a2-6506eb22170d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Genetic correlations", "children": [], "description": "Genetic correlations identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within quantitative traits. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After breeder’s equation, genetic correlations supplies what is needed to address plasticity."}, {"id": "2357fa1b-1564-41cd-9fd1-0d85795cf11e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Plasticity", "children": [], "description": "Plasticity identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within quantitative traits. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, plasticity carries the completed idea into phylogenetics."}]}, {"id": "c605534c-e49b-41c6-a4cc-3a340d94a77e", "type": "topic", "title": "Phylogenetics", "description": "This module builds directly on quantitative traits and develops phylogenetics. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for molecular evolution.", "children": [{"id": "119f7898-ecb1-4e5f-af42-2f5966d95770", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Characters", "children": [], "description": "Characters identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within phylogenetics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before homology because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "4e7c5540-a6b2-41a9-9f56-65c6ea317843", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Homology", "children": [], "description": "Homology identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within phylogenetics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After characters, homology supplies what is needed to address tree thinking."}, {"id": "19327fb1-b18a-46fc-902b-4cfc871e4fea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tree thinking", "children": [], "description": "Tree thinking identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within phylogenetics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After homology, tree thinking supplies what is needed to address parsimony/likelihood concepts."}, {"id": "4e31224c-1c83-451f-afdd-596933b048fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Parsimony/likelihood concepts", "children": [], "description": "Parsimony/likelihood concepts is a governing quantity in phylogenetics, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. As the final topic in this module, parsimony/likelihood concepts carries the completed idea into molecular evolution."}]}, {"id": "71c56413-cc45-4f5c-8c16-95ff3da87bf1", "type": "topic", "title": "Molecular evolution", "description": "This module builds directly on phylogenetics and develops molecular evolution. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for species and speciation.", "children": [{"id": "f944824e-47fe-4d51-8577-1c9579c45d3a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Substitution", "children": [], "description": "Substitution supplies the causal sequence within molecular evolution, which is necessary for predicting unfamiliar outcomes instead of memorizing examples. It appears before neutral theory because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "79e85eae-9161-4b51-b895-df7a7c48aa80", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Neutral theory", "children": [], "description": "Neutral theory identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within molecular evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After substitution, neutral theory supplies what is needed to address clocks."}, {"id": "37b53e4b-2b59-4c2d-bd1e-b937a1dadcd2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clocks", "children": [], "description": "Clocks identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within molecular evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After neutral theory, clocks supplies what is needed to address genome evolution."}, {"id": "87123fe9-4635-4993-9e97-89d8ff5a283c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Genome evolution", "children": [], "description": "Genome evolution identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within molecular evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, genome evolution carries the completed idea into species and speciation."}]}, {"id": "77ed8523-929a-418a-9859-d88cb847cfbd", "type": "topic", "title": "Species and speciation", "description": "This module builds directly on molecular evolution and develops species and speciation. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for coevolution and social evolution.", "children": [{"id": "d0ee1815-4ae1-4416-a347-b2b42d79a949", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reproductive isolation", "children": [], "description": "Reproductive isolation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within species and speciation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before geographic modes because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "35313600-68ca-412c-b038-aea387c757b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Geographic modes", "children": [], "description": "Geographic modes identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within species and speciation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After reproductive isolation, geographic modes supplies what is needed to address hybridization."}, {"id": "2438fe0b-0293-4dce-ad96-cf2898e0e5ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hybridization", "children": [], "description": "Hybridization identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within species and speciation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, hybridization carries the completed idea into coevolution and social evolution."}]}, {"id": "22c4df59-e93a-4a52-99f0-18d7e5fa2cc3", "type": "topic", "title": "Coevolution and social evolution", "description": "This module builds directly on species and speciation and develops coevolution and social evolution. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for macroevolution and human evolution.", "children": [{"id": "399d8ed9-bd12-474a-a0cc-fa318f3e4b14", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Arms races", "children": [], "description": "Arms races identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within coevolution and social evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before kin selection because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "147a4e1d-f9ea-402a-bec3-90bad6f860e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Kin selection", "children": [], "description": "Kin selection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within coevolution and social evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After arms races, kin selection supplies what is needed to address cooperation."}, {"id": "f0d8f18a-d9d3-4dd7-93b8-7e5ae768c54c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cooperation", "children": [], "description": "Cooperation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within coevolution and social evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After kin selection, cooperation supplies what is needed to address sexual selection."}, {"id": "8de8507d-5329-4f2f-b3f7-477b3e261839", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sexual selection", "children": [], "description": "Sexual selection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within coevolution and social evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, sexual selection carries the completed idea into macroevolution and human evolution."}]}, {"id": "e4464643-7cf4-45c7-a6a3-61f47ba43c9f", "type": "topic", "title": "Macroevolution and human evolution", "description": "This culminating module draws on coevolution and social evolution and develops macroevolution and human evolution. It belongs last because it requires the earlier tools to be selected, combined, and evaluated rather than used one at a time.", "children": [{"id": "4230471d-fbe8-4ed8-bd54-669948a52092", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diversification", "children": [], "description": "Diversification identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within macroevolution and human evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before extinction because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "df767472-803f-4655-998e-e2af6fc40d0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Extinction", "children": [], "description": "Extinction identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within macroevolution and human evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After diversification, extinction supplies what is needed to address developmental evolution."}, {"id": "5db0a96a-0272-4e3a-aa80-0370de55328b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Developmental evolution", "children": [], "description": "Developmental evolution identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within macroevolution and human evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After extinction, developmental evolution supplies what is needed to address synthesis."}, {"id": "75f7efff-5a8a-4166-919c-cdba2fa32a89", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Synthesis", "children": [], "description": "Synthesis turns the theory of macroevolution and human evolution into a defensible decision and exposes the relevant structure, cost, or performance trade-offs. As the final course topic, synthesis requires ideas from the complete path to be integrated and transferred."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$evobiozzjs$::jsonb,
