 "subtopic", "title": "Homology", "children": [], "description": "Homology identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within phylogenetics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After characters, homology supplies what is needed to address tree thinking."}, {"id": "19327fb1-b18a-46fc-902b-4cfc871e4fea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tree thinking", "children": [], "description": "Tree thinking identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within phylogenetics. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After homology, tree thinking supplies what is needed to address parsimony/likelihood concepts."}, {"id": "4e31224c-1c83-451f-afdd-596933b048fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Parsimony/likelihood concepts", "children": [], "description": "Parsimony/likelihood concepts is a governing quantity in phylogenetics, linking local calculations to system-level behavior and offering a consistency check. As the final topic in this module, parsimony/likelihood concepts carries the completed idea into molecular evolution."}]}, {"id": "71c56413-cc45-4f5c-8c16-95ff3da87bf1", "type": "topic", "title": "Molecular evolution", "description": "This module builds directly on phylogenetics and develops molecular evolution. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for species and speciation.", "children": [{"id": "f944824e-47fe-4d51-8577-1c9579c45d3a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Substitution", "children": [], "description": "Substitution supplies the causal sequence within molecular evolution, which is necessary for predicting unfamiliar outcomes instead of memorizing examples. It appears before neutral theory because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "79e85eae-9161-4b51-b895-df7a7c48aa80", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Neutral theory", "children": [], "description": "Neutral theory identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within molecular evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After substitution, neutral theory supplies what is needed to address clocks."}, {"id": "37b53e4b-2b59-4c2d-bd1e-b937a1dadcd2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Clocks", "children": [], "description": "Clocks identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within molecular evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After neutral theory, clocks supplies what is needed to address genome evolution."}, {"id": "87123fe9-4635-4993-9e97-89d8ff5a283c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Genome evolution", "children": [], "description": "Genome evolution identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within molecular evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, genome evolution carries the completed idea into species and speciation."}]}, {"id": "77ed8523-929a-418a-9859-d88cb847cfbd", "type": "topic", "title": "Species and speciation", "description": "This module builds directly on molecular evolution and develops species and speciation. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for coevolution and social evolution.", "children": [{"id": "d0ee1815-4ae1-4416-a347-b2b42d79a949", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reproductive isolation", "children": [], "description": "Reproductive isolation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within species and speciation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before geographic modes because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "35313600-68ca-412c-b038-aea387c757b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Geographic modes", "children": [], "description": "Geographic modes identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within species and speciation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After reproductive isolation, geographic modes supplies what is needed to address hybridization."}, {"id": "2438fe0b-0293-4dce-ad96-cf2898e0e5ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hybridization", "children": [], "description": "Hybridization identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within species and speciation. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, hybridization carries the completed idea into coevolution and social evolution."}]}, {"id": "22c4df59-e93a-4a52-99f0-18d7e5fa2cc3", "type": "topic", "title": "Coevolution and social evolution", "description": "This module builds directly on species and speciation and develops coevolution and social evolution. It belongs here because its methods and distinctions are prerequisites for macroevolution and human evolution.", "children": [{"id": "399d8ed9-bd12-474a-a0cc-fa318f3e4b14", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Arms races", "children": [], "description": "Arms races identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within coevolution and social evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before kin selection because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "147a4e1d-f9ea-402a-bec3-90bad6f860e0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Kin selection", "children": [], "description": "Kin selection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within coevolution and social evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After arms races, kin selection supplies what is needed to address cooperation."}, {"id": "f0d8f18a-d9d3-4dd7-93b8-7e5ae768c54c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cooperation", "children": [], "description": "Cooperation identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within coevolution and social evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After kin selection, cooperation supplies what is needed to address sexual selection."}, {"id": "8de8507d-5329-4f2f-b3f7-477b3e261839", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sexual selection", "children": [], "description": "Sexual selection identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within coevolution and social evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. As the final topic in this module, sexual selection carries the completed idea into macroevolution and human evolution."}]}, {"id": "e4464643-7cf4-45c7-a6a3-61f47ba43c9f", "type": "topic", "title": "Macroevolution and human evolution", "description": "This culminating module draws on coevolution and social evolution and develops macroevolution and human evolution. It belongs last because it requires the earlier tools to be selected, combined, and evaluated rather than used one at a time.", "children": [{"id": "4230471d-fbe8-4ed8-bd54-669948a52092", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diversification", "children": [], "description": "Diversification identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within macroevolution and human evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. It appears before extinction because that next topic assumes this starting point."}, {"id": "df767472-803f-4655-998e-e2af6fc40d0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Extinction", "children": [], "description": "Extinction identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within macroevolution and human evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After diversification, extinction supplies what is needed to address developmental evolution."}, {"id": "5db0a96a-0272-4e3a-aa80-0370de55328b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Developmental evolution", "children": [], "description": "Developmental evolution identifies a specific object, distinction, or relationship within macroevolution and human evolution. Learners need to recognize and use it before combining this module's ideas in later work. After extinction, developmental evolution supplies what is needed to address synthesis."}, {"id": "75f7efff-5a8a-4166-919c-cdba2fa32a89", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Synthesis", "children": [], "description": "Synthesis turns the theory of macroevolution and human evolution into a defensible decision and exposes the relevant structure, cost, or performance trade-offs. As the final course topic, synthesis requires ideas from the complete path to be integrated and transferred."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$evobiozzjs$::jsonb,
